*---------------------------------------------------------------
* mm.procbnk2.equ -- the rest of the process-bank layout
* (docs/MEMMAP.md #3): process ZP/stack/low-free, the packed
* argv string region and its two derived ceilings, the heap top,
* the $BF00 overlay page, process LC storage, and
* the $FFxx page's internal stub layout (dum'd at its real
* address). Split out of inc/memmap.equ (docs/SELFHOST-
* CONVERSION.md phase 1) -- kept separate from the tiny, nearly-
* universal inc/mm.procbank.equ because only
* spawn/lazy-free kernel code and the kernel-bearing test
* manifests need this half; ordinary userland programs (echo,
* cat, ls, ...) never do. Requires inc/mm.procbank.equ
* PUT first: ARG_MAX below derives from LOAD_BASE.
* Full design notes: I.MEMMAPE.TXT (docs/a2/), docs/MEMMAP.md #3
*---------------------------------------------------------------

PRC_ZP         equ   $0000       ;256B process ZP
PRC_STACK      equ   $0100       ;256B process stack
PRC_LOWFREE    equ   $0200       ;1536B free low process space,
                                  ;no display hole in banks != 0

PRC_ARGV_STR   equ   $0300       ;packed NUL-terminated strings
                                  ;-- argv's, THEN envp's

* -- SUSTAINABILITY NOTE 2026-08-25 (operator: "I wonder if the
* -- page3 thing is sustainable"). Not a bug, not scheduled --
* -- pinned so it is not rediscovered. Two distinct worries:
* --
* -- 1. THE WINDOW CANNOT GROW. It is walled by the stack below
* --    and LOAD_BASE above, and ARG_MAX is DERIVED, not chosen.
* --    Growing it means lowering PRC_ARGV_STR (eating the
* --    pointer array) or raising LOAD_BASE (relocating every
* --    binary -- liba bytes are volume bytes, ~40 gate images).
* --    Meanwhile tenancy grows: argv alone -> argv+envp
* --    (2026-08-22, numbers unchanged, COVERAGE doubled) -> the
* --    subshell design went looking for a third tenant and
* --    found nowhere. The trend points one way.
* --
* -- 2. PAGE 3 IS THE MOST CONTESTED PAGE ON AN APPLE II. Period
* --    software treats $0300 as scratch and $03D0-$03FF is
* --    DOS/ProDOS vector territory. In an aux bank it is plain
* --    RAM, so this is free TODAY -- but task #8 is self-
* --    hosting: real Merlin-8 making period assumptions in a
* --    process bank whose $0300 holds live argv strings. That
* --    assumption was written down NOWHERE before this note
* --    (grepped docs/MEMMAP.md and the selfhost docs).
* --
* --    AND PAGE 2 IS NO BETTER (operator, 2026-08-30): $0200
* --    is the ROM's keyboard input buffer -- GETLN/READLN read
* --    lines INTO $0200-$02FF -- which is exactly where the
* --    argv header and pointer array sit. Not hypothetical:
* --    real Merlin-8's core uses $0200 as its console buffer
* --    and WORKSP=$0280 for PUT filenames, in the SAME bank
* --    where `as` staged its own argv. Sequenced-safe today
* --    only because `as` finishes with argv before invoking
* --    the core; any period code calling ROM READLN in a
* --    process bank scribbles the startup frame. maux's own
* --    kernel/liba never touch $0200 (grepped 2026-08-30).
* --    One more weight on the BETTER FORM below: args above
* --    the image leave $0200-$07FF to the period software
* --    that believes it owns it.
* --
* -- ESCAPE HATCH, if it ever bites: stage low as now, then have
* -- crt0 relocate argv/envp into the heap and release the
* -- window. One copy, size unbounded, PCB_BRK already exists.
* --
* -- BETTER FORM, operator same day ("once argv and envp are in
* -- the heap (well, under the BRK) size concerns change"): do
* -- not transit through the low window at all. The kernel
* -- stages argv/envp immediately ABOVE the image and sets
* -- PCB_BRK past them rather than zeroing it, so the strings
* -- land inside [LOAD_BASE, brk) below the program's initial
* -- break and sbrk grows from there. No crt0 copy, no transit
* -- buffer -- and a transit buffer would have kept the 1280 B
* -- ceiling anyway, since transit capacity IS the limit. The
* -- low window is then freed outright: 1536 B back per bank,
* -- and worry 2 above DISSOLVES rather than being managed.
* -- fork needs no change (procfork.s:17 already copies
* -- [PRC_LOWFREE, PCB_BRK*256) -- the block just moves from the
* -- low end of that range into the middle); lazy-free already
* -- restages. Item 13c's rule that the kernel does the ERR_2BIG
* -- check survives: the kernel knows the image length.
* --
* -- TWO COSTS, so this is not free:
* --
* -- a. THE CEILING WOULD GO PER-PROGRAM, which is real Unix
* --    drift -- ARG_MAX is a system constant you can query, and
* --    a command line that works with echo failing with as is
* --    exactly the non-obvious divergence the house rule
* --    forbids. Not forced, though: publish a conservative
* --    CONSTANT floor (4 KB, say) always available regardless
* --    of image size and refuse above it. ARG_MAX stays a
* --    constant, simply tripled. The relocation buys the
* --    FREEDOM to pick a bigger number; picking one keeps the
* --    contract.
* --
* -- b. PCB_BRK == 0 MEANS "UNSET" and that is load-bearing in
* --    three places (SCH_CREATE zeroes it, procfork.s:439 calls
* --    that "right for spawn", lazy-free zeroes it on reuse).
* --    Pre-setting it to image+args changes that invariant.
* --
* -- AND ONE THING GETS BETTER: the environment-reuse idea
* -- (docs/SYSCALL.md item 13c note, same day) wants to know
* -- whether a warm bank already holds the right environment.
* -- Same program -> same image length -> staged block at the
* -- SAME address, so the generation tag has a fixed place to
* -- compare instead of a moving one.
* -- NEITHER FORM IS RULED OUT BY ITEM 13c, though the order
* -- above makes it look that way. 13c rejected the heap for
* -- staging because it does not exist when the kernel must
* -- stage. That is correct, and it kills neither: the FIRST
* -- form relocates AFTER start, when the heap does exist; the
* -- SECOND does not wait for a heap at all, because the kernel
* -- SETS the initial break itself rather than finding one.
* --
* -- ARG_MAX's CEILING is gated (check_argv.py, e2e_limits.py).
* -- What is unmeasured is HEADROOM: how close real spawns get.
* -- That is the cheap first move if this starts feeling live.
* See I.MEMMAPE.TXT: "ARG_MAX -- the spawn() argument-list"
* -- BOTH ceilings became COMBINED budgets on 2026-08-22
* -- (docs/SYSCALL.md item 13c): the environment shares this
* -- block with argv, so ARG_MAX bounds argv's strings PLUS
* -- envp's, and ARGV_PTR_LIM bounds argv's pointers PLUS the
* -- envc byte PLUS envp's pointers. The numbers did not move --
* -- what they cover did. spawn() still returns ERR_2BIG rather
* -- than staging a prefix, so a program that started at all can
* -- trust that argv AND environment are complete.
ARG_MAX        equ   LOAD_BASE-PRC_ARGV_STR
                                  ;1280B of packed strings,
                                  ;NULs included
ARGV_PTR_LIM   equ   PRC_ARGV_STR-PRC_ARGV_PTRS
                                  ;255B of pointer array -> 127
                                  ;entries max, the count that
                                  ;used to be declared
PRC_HEAP_TOP   equ   $BEFF       ;top of sbrk-managed heap
                                  ;(below overlay)
BF00_OVERLAY    equ   $BF00       ;256B reserved-but-optional
                                  ;MLI overlay pg

* -- PRC_BRK_LIM -- the highest LEGAL break (src/kernel/
* -- process.s PRC_BRK, 2026-08-22). A break is the address
* -- ONE PAST the heap, so a break of $BF00 owns through
* -- $BEFF == PRC_HEAP_TOP and stops exactly below the overlay
* -- page. Deliberately spelled as BF00_OVERLAY rather than
* -- PRC_HEAP_TOP+1: real Merlin-8 has no parentheses and
* -- evaluates strictly left to right, so a caller writing
* -- `lda #<PRC_HEAP_TOP+1` is one dialect trap away from
* -- $00 instead of the intended low byte
* -- (learning:01M051DJW89KV4JYM1EC9SDZ5Y). The kernel keeps
* -- the break as a PAGE NUMBER (see PCB_BRK,
* -- inc/mm.annex.equ), so only >PRC_BRK_LIM is ever
* -- compared against.
PRC_BRK_LIM     equ   BF00_OVERLAY

* SB_WINDOW REMOVED 2026-08-22 (docs/STICKY.md sec 25): it named
* the $0800-$BEFF span a CACHED image had to fit inside, and
* lazy free has no cache -- a retained bank IS a process bank,
* so the only span that matters is the one PRC_BRK_LIM already
* bounds. Recorded rather than silently dropped, the same way
* INODE_*'s removal is recorded in inc/mm.annex.equ.
PRC_IO_SLTROM equ   $C000       ;4096B never process memory --
                                  ;refused by copyin/copyout
                                  ;outright
PRC_LC_BANK1   equ   $D000       ;4096B process LC storage,
                                  ;bank 1
PRC_LC_BANK2   equ   $D000       ;4096B process LC storage,
                                  ;bank 2 (DEFAULT target of the
                                  ;ALTZP-aware copy path -- see
                                  ;LC_DFLT_BANK below)
PRC_LC_COMMON  equ   $E000       ;7936B process LC storage,
                                  ;common
FFXX_PAGE       equ   $FF00       ;256B -- the kernel's ONLY
                                  ;claim in a native bank; see
                                  ;below

LC_DFLT_BANK equ   2           ;the cold-read finding: ALTZP-
                                  ;aware copyin/ copyout always
                                  ;explicitly selects bank 2
                                  ;before touching process LC
                                  ;memory (never trusts ambient
                                  ;bank-1/2 latch state)

* -- 3.3 $FFxx page internal layout (dum'd at its real, absolute
* address --
*    every label here IS the address code jumps/vectors to) --
            dum   $FF00
SYSCALL_ENTRY   ds    20          ;JSR $FF00 syscall door
IRQ_ENTRY       ds    14          ;$FFFE-vectored IRQ/BRK door
EXIT_TAIL       ds    12          ;shared exit tail, both doors
BANK_ID         ds    1           ;per-bank identity byte (PCB
                                  ;per-bank half)
FFXX_SCRATCH    ds    5           ;reserved per-bank kernel
                                  ;scratch
NMI_TRAP        ds    2           ;BRA * -- NMI ruled out, parks
                                  ;for debugger
RESET_STUB      ds    6           ;defensive-only; real recovery
                                  ;is $03F2
FFXX_SLACK      ds    190         ;unused -- headroom for task
                                  ;#3
NMI_VEC         equ   $FFFA
RESET_VEC       equ   $FFFC
IRQ_VEC         equ   $FFFE
            dend
* Budget check: 20+14+12+1+5+2+6 = 60 stub bytes + 190 slack =
* 250 usable, + 6 hardware-vector bytes = 256 = the whole page.
* 60 of 250 used.
